      "text": "Shamrock Colony was established in 2007 as a daughter colony of the nearby Huron Hutterite Colony in Beadle County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shamrock_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community follows Hutterite principles of shared property, pacifism, and plain dress to maintain a communal lifestyle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shamrock_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Shamrock Colony Elementary School provides public education for grades K through 8 in this remote rural setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shamrock_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Founding members of Shamrock Colony split livestock, machinery, and financial assets from their parent colony to ensure immediate self-sufficiency.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shamrock_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Shamrock Colony occupies about zero point six square miles of communal farmland in the east-central part of South Dakota.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shamrock_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Winters in Shamrock Colony often bring below-freezing conditions and occasional blizzards, while summers are typically warm and humid.",
